course: dictionary
lesson: 4340
title: Guardian: one word, several jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A guardian is a person or thing that protects or looks after something. Read the words around the word to find out which meaning fits. The clues in the sentence tell you whether the guardian is a person, an animal or an angel.
explain: «In Australia the ratings include ... MA15+ (under-15s must be with a parent or guardian)» Here the clue is parent. A guardian is an adult who looks after a young person, just as a parent does.
explain: «Livestock guardian dogs grow up with sheep ... barking at and chasing away foxes» Here the guardian is an animal. Test your meaning: swap in protector and read the sentence again. It still makes sense, so guardian means protector here.
fact: Guardian means a person or thing that protects or guards something.
fact: A legal guardian is an adult who is responsible for looking after a child who is not their own, for example when the parents have died or cannot care for the child.
fact: A guardian angel is, in some Christian beliefs, an angel who watches over each person.
fact: «Livestock guardian dogs» bark at and chase away foxes and other predators, often at night.
exercise: «In the USA ... R (under-17s need a parent or guardian with them)» What does guardian mean in this sentence? | A law about cinemas | *An adult who looks after a young person | A sheep that guards the farm | A film that is very scary
exercise: «Livestock guardian dogs grow up with sheep and treat them as their family.» What is the guardian in this sentence? | A farmer who sells the sheep | *A dog that protects the sheep | A fox that hides at night | A sheep that sleeps all day
exercise: What is a guardian angel? | A bird that sings at night | A teacher who runs the school | *An angel who watches over each person, in some Christian beliefs | A soldier who guards a castle gate
test: After her parents died, Ella's aunt became her legal guardian. What does this tell you? | *Her aunt is legally responsible for looking after her | Ella lives alone in a flat | Her aunt works as a postwoman | Her aunt is a famous singer
test: The old oak tree is the guardian of the forest. What does guardian mean here? | Map of the paths | Visitor | *Protector | Tallest tree
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to guardian, when it means a protector? | Visitor | Stranger | Enemy | *Protector
